<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36610" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plausĭbĭlis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		plaudo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>deserving applause</i>, <i>praiseworthy</i>, <i>acceptable</i>, <i>pleasing</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">censorium nomen (with populare),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. in Caecil. 3, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oratio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen.
					Ep. 5, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">locus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint.
					4, 3, 1</span></i>
			.—Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plau-sĭbĭlĭter</span></b> , <i>with applause</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ingenium plausibilius manifestare,</span>”
				<i>with more applause</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 8, 10</span></i>
			.</div>
